        "optionB": "Absence of density-dependent regulation",
        "optionC": "Large body size, long life span and few offspring with parental care",
        "optionD": "Early maturity and many small offspring",
        "correctOption": "C",
        "analysisA": "Incorrect. High r is a feature of r-selected species.",
        "analysisB": "Incorrect. K-selected species are strongly regulated by density-dependent factors.",
        "analysisC": "Correct. K-selected species (e.g., elephants, large trees) live near carrying capacity.",
        "analysisD": "Incorrect. This describes r-selected species such as weeds and insects.",
        "referenceNote": "Syllabus reference: Unit-8 > Species and Population Ecology: life history strategies (r and K selection)\nThe r-K selection theory was proposed by MacArthur and Wilson.",
