        "sNo": 8,
        "question": "In xerarch succession on a bare rock (lithosere), the pioneer community consists of:",
        "optionA": "Climax trees",
        "optionB": "Shrubs",
        "optionC": "Mosses",
        "optionD": "Crustose lichens",
        "correctOption": "D",
        "analysisA": "Incorrect. Climax trees form the final stable community.",
        "analysisB": "Incorrect. Shrubs arrive in later seral stages.",
        "analysisC": "Incorrect. Mosses follow lichens and trap soil.",
        "analysisD": "Correct. Crustose lichens secrete acids that weather rock, forming the first soil.",
        "referenceNote": "Syllabus reference: Unit-8 > Community Ecology: ecological succession\nSuccession: nudation, invasion, competition, reaction, stabilisation (climax).",
        "isValid": true,
        "errors": []
